---
// The teardowns index. Teardowns are the one page kind with a shelf life: the project plan caps how many
// may be live and expires each one after `expires_days`, so this page prints both numbers and
// separates the live ones from any that have passed their date, rather than quietly listing a
// teardown of a product that may have changed since it was decoded.
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionTop from '../../components/SectionTop.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/url';
import {
  teardowns,
  teardownCap,
  teardownExpiryDays,
  techniquesForTeardown,
  teardownExpiry,
  teardownIsStale,
} from '../../lib/content';

const rows = await Promise.all(
  teardowns.map(async (t) => {
    const entry = await getEntry('teardowns', t.slug);
    const reviewed = entry ? entry.data.reviewed.toISOString().slice(0, 10) : undefined;
    const techniques = techniquesForTeardown(t);
    const levels = [
      ...new Set(techniques.map((x) => x.level).filter((l): l is number => typeof l === 'number')),
    ].sort((a, b) => a - b);
    return {
      slug: t.slug,
      title: t.title,
      techniques,
      levels,
      reviewed,
      expires: reviewed ? teardownExpiry(reviewed) : undefined,
      stale: reviewed ? teardownIsStale(reviewed) : false,
    };
  }),
);

const live = rows.filter((r) => !r.stale);
const expired = rows.filter((r) => r.stale);
---
<Base
  title="Teardowns · Gradient Ascent"
  description="A product you have used, taken apart into the techniques it is built from: what you see, what runs underneath, and which page explains each part."
>
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow muted"><span class="dot"></span>Teardowns</div>
    <h1>Products you have used, taken apart</h1>
    <p>
      A teardown starts from something a reader has already used and works downward: what you see,
      what is happening underneath level by level, which technique page explains each part, what
      the maker says about how theirs works, and where it fails. Every claim about a product is
      what its own maker documents.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <SectionTop
      eyebrow="Live teardowns"
      title={`${live.length} of ${teardownCap} live`}
      aside={`A teardown dates faster than a technique does, so each one expires ${teardownExpiryDays} days after it was last reviewed and is re-reviewed or retired then. At most ${teardownCap} are live at once.`}
    />
    <div class="signal-list">
      {
        live.map((r) => (
          <div class="signal-row">
            <div class="signal-layer">
              {r.levels.map((l) => (
                <i style={`--c:var(--o${l})`} />
              ))}
              <span>{r.levels.length ? r.levels.map((l) => `Level ${l}`).join(' + ') : 'Topics'}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="signal-body">
              <h3>
                <a href={url(`/teardowns/${r.slug}/`)}>{r.title}</a>
              </h3>
              <p>{r.techniques.map((t) => t.title).join(' · ')}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="signal-meta">
              {r.reviewed ? `Reviewed ${r.reviewed}` : 'Not written yet'}
              {r.expires && <><br />Expires {r.expires}</>}
            </div>
            <a href={url(`/teardowns/${r.slug}/`)} aria-label={`Open ${r.title}`}>
              &#8599;
            </a>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  {
    expired.length > 0 && (
      <section class="section">
        <SectionTop
          eyebrow="Past their date"
          title={`${expired.length} waiting for a re-review`}
          aside="These are still readable, but a product may have changed since. They do not count against the live cap and are not linked from technique pages until they are re-reviewed."
        />
        <div class="signal-list">
          {expired.map((r) => (
            <div class="signal-row">
              <div class="signal-layer">
                <span>Stale</span>
              </div>
              <div class="signal-body">
                <h3>
                  <a href={url(`/teardowns/${r.slug}/`)}>{r.title}</a>
                </h3>
                <p>{r.techniques.map((t) => t.title).join(' · ')}</p>
              </div>
              <div class="signal-meta">Expired {r.expires}</div>
              <a href={url(`/teardowns/${r.slug}/`)} aria-label={`Open ${r.title}`}>
                &#8599;
              </a>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    )
  }

  <p class="footnote reading">
    A teardown is one of the three layers in the project plan's content model, under the techniques
    themselves and beside the <a href={url('/recipes/')} style="color:var(--accent)">recipes</a>.
    How to write one is in <code>docs/WRITING-A-TEARDOWN.md</code>.
  </p>
</Base>
